NextSQL
=======

Encrypted-by-default multimodel database. This archive contains:

  bin/nextsql         CLI (init, exec, migrate, backup, …)
  bin/nextsqld        Server (NSQL v1 protocol, default 127.0.0.1:7210)
  bin/nextsql-bench   Official measurements (encryption, WAL, fsync on)
  etc/nextsql.conf    Default nextsqld --config file
  systemd/            Unit, sysusers, tmpfiles
  install.sh          System-wide or user-local installer
  uninstall.sh

Install (system-wide, as root):

  sudo ./install.sh

Install into $HOME/.local (no root):

  ./install.sh --user

Then initialize a data directory. Keep the root unlock key off the data
volume in production.

  printf 'secret\n' > /tmp/nextsql.pw && chmod 600 /tmp/nextsql.pw
  nextsql init --data-dir /var/lib/nextsql --key-file /etc/nextsql/root.key \
    --user app --password-file /tmp/nextsql.pw
  sudo systemctl enable --now nextsql     # system install

User-local data and key paths are printed by install.sh --user.

Loopback may run without TLS. Any other listen address requires TLS 1.3.

https://github.com/bzync/nextsql
